WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.793
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.093 --> 00:00:08.108
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:15.472
Unit twenty-four: Entrepreneurship. In this unit, you will discuss starting businesses and past regrets.

4
00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.345
venture.

5
00:00:18.045 --> 00:00:21.159
venture means a new business activity that involves risk.

6
00:00:21.459 --> 00:00:23.470
Their new venture sells handmade soap.

7
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.033
Your turn. Say: venture.

8
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:29.630
venture.

9
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:31.664
start-up capital.

10
00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:35.513
start-up capital means the money needed to start a business.

11
00:00:35.813 --> 00:00:38.115
They used their savings as start-up capital.

12
00:00:38.815 --> 00:00:41.490
Your turn. Say: start-up capital.

13
00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.690
start-up capital.

14
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:47.661
business model.

15
00:00:48.361 --> 00:00:51.139
business model means how a company plans to make money.

16
00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:54.112
Their business model is based on subscriptions.

17
00:00:54.812 --> 00:00:57.127
Your turn. Say: business model.

18
00:00:59.827 --> 00:01:01.049
business model.

19
00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.214
market research.

20
00:01:03.914 --> 00:01:07.631
market research means collecting information about what customers want.

21
00:01:07.931 --> 00:01:10.697
Market research showed demand for healthy snacks.

22
00:01:11.397 --> 00:01:14.259
Your turn. Say: market research.

23
00:01:16.959 --> 00:01:18.331
market research.

24
00:01:19.317 --> 00:01:20.260
crowdfunding.

25
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.283
crowdfunding means raising money from many people online.

26
00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:27.662
The project raised $10,000 through crowdfunding.

27
00:01:28.362 --> 00:01:30.480
Your turn. Say: crowdfunding.

28
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.286
crowdfunding.

29
00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:36.528
angel investor.

30
00:01:37.228 --> 00:01:41.283
angel investor means a rich person who invests in new small businesses.

31
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:43.849
An angel investor believed in her idea.

32
00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:46.784
Your turn. Say: angel investor.

33
00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:50.972
angel investor.

34
00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:52.822
scale up.

35
00:01:53.522 --> 00:01:56.404
scale up means to grow a business to a bigger size.

36
00:01:56.704 --> 00:01:59.017
They plan to scale up to five cities.

37
00:01:59.717 --> 00:02:01.696
Your turn. Say: scale up.

38
00:02:04.396 --> 00:02:05.258
scale up.

39
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.089
revenue.

40
00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:10.868
revenue means the money a business receives from sales.

41
00:02:11.168 --> 00:02:13.074
Revenue doubled in the second year.

42
00:02:13.774 --> 00:02:15.753
Your turn. Say: revenue.

43
00:02:18.453 --> 00:02:19.408
revenue.

44
00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:22.416
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:22.716 --> 00:02:24.402
How's your friend's start-up going?

46
00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:30.784
Not great. If she had done more market research, she wouldn't have chosen that location.

47
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:33.909
What happened with the start-up capital?

48
00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:39.552
She used her savings. If she'd tried crowdfunding, she might have found more.

49
00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.000
Did any angel investor show interest?

50
00:02:44.317 --> 00:02:49.561
One did, but she refused. She wishes she hadn't! They could have scaled up together.

51
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:54.080
Grammar focus: Third conditional and regrets.

52
00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.110
Use the third conditional to imagine a different past and its result.

53
00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.048
Use wish plus past perfect to express regret.

54
00:03:01.348 --> 00:03:06.937
For example: If she had done research, she would have chosen better. I wish I had accepted the offer.

55
00:03:07.237 --> 00:03:10.688
Contracted forms are common in speech: If I'd known, I'd have helped.

56
00:03:11.683 --> 00:03:14.661
Now read and listen. What Founders Wish They'd Known.

57
00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.901
Most new ventures fail within their first five years.

58
00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:22.702
Many founders say they wish they had done more market research.

59
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:27.154
Others admit that their business model wasn't clear enough.

60
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.632
If they had found an angel investor earlier, some could have scaled up successfully.

61
00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:38.192
Learning from these stories can help new entrepreneurs grow their revenue faster.

62
00:03:39.483 --> 00:03:41.985
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:42.285 --> 00:03:44.760
Money needed to start a business is blank.

64
00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.528
A, revenue. B, start-up capital. C, venture.

65
00:03:52.517 --> 00:03:54.563
The answer is B: start-up capital.

66
00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.212
If I blank harder, I would have passed.

67
00:03:58.512 --> 00:04:01.898
A, studied. B, had studied. C, would study.

68
00:04:05.883 --> 00:04:07.871
The answer is B: had studied.

69
00:04:09.383 --> 00:04:12.558
I wish I blank that job. It was a great opportunity.

70
00:04:12.858 --> 00:04:15.594
A, took. B, had taken. C, take.

71
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:21.420
The answer is B: had taken.

72
00:04:22.917 --> 00:04:25.497
Raising money from many people online is blank.

73
00:04:25.797 --> 00:04:29.949
A, crowdfunding. B, market research. C, scale up.

74
00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:36.228
The answer is A: crowdfunding.

75
00:04:37.717 --> 00:04:41.585
According to the text, many founders wish they had done more blank.

76
00:04:41.885 --> 00:04:45.771
A, advertising. B, market research. C, travelling.

77
00:04:49.783 --> 00:04:52.352
The answer is B: market research.

78
00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:58.513
Now it's your turn to speak. Is there a decision you regret? What would have happened differently?

79
00:05:03.813 --> 00:05:09.424
If I had started learning English earlier, I would have had more job opportunities after university.

80
00:05:09.724 --> 00:05:11.189
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:12.183 --> 00:05:16.124
Great work today! You learned eight new words and third conditional and regrets.

82
00:05:16.424 --> 00:05:20.052
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

83
00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:23.329
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

84
00:05:23.629 --> 00:05:26.549
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

